  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Towards Malaria Elimination (TOME)  - Leveraging Local Capacity to Strengthen Health Service Delivery Project (LLCAP) - Malaria Case Management</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Malawi):  USAID&apos;s Leveraging Local Capacity to Strengthen Health Service Delivery  - Towards Malaria Elimination activity will increase the percentage of  suspected malaria cases tested, confirmed cases treated, uptake of intermittent preventive treatment in pregnancy, and strengthen the malaria surveillance system to guide program implementation and accountability. In order to achieve these outcomes, the activity will use FY 2022 funds to: 1) train healthcare workers and health surveillance assistants in malaria prevention and case management; 2) develop and distribute tools including job aids to healthcare workers and disease surveillance assistants; 3) provide technical assistance to strengthen quality assurance, supply chain, and surveillance systems; and 4) work with local organizations to increase the practice of positive malaria prevention and control behaviors...By reducing malaria burden in targeted districts, the  activity enhances Malawi&apos;s pathway to locally led development and aligns with the Integrated Country Strategy Mission Objective 3.2 - Malawi improves access to and quality of health services so that more of its citizens gain and retain full health and can contribute productively at home, in the community, and at work. The activity further supports the Joint Strategic Plan Objective 1.1: Strengthen global health security, combat infectious disease threats, and address priority global health challenges through bilateral engagement and within multilateral fora...</narrative>
  </description>
